      "writtenOn": "2026-04-29T15:27:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The changes in `driver/fingerprint/egis/egis_api.h` are nearly identical to `zephyr/drivers/fingerprint/fingerprint_egis630_private.h`.\n\nIssue: Maintaining two identical headers for the same API increases the likelihood of them diverging during future maintenance.\n\nRecommendation: If possible, have the Zephyr driver include the central Egis header rather than duplicating the entire API definition and comments.",
      "revId": "d88db1fba163aca7fb6aee481250a27e2a450f3a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "405f666f_bb6684c9",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1541085
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-29T15:33:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "was the zephyr test issue resolved? Is so, how?",
      "revId": "d88db1fba163aca7fb6aee481250a27e2a450f3a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "64c7433d_0daf290b",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 3698372
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-30T04:24:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, they are nearly identical, but strictly speaking they serve two different\nimplementations.\n\n`egis_api.h` targets the legacy EC path, while\n`fingerprint_egis630_private.h` is specific to the Zephyr EC implementation.\nThey happen to look very similar because both consume the same private Egis\nlibrary, which defines the underlying interface and semantics.\n\nThis separation is consistent with other vendors as well. For example, the `Elan` driver follows the same pattern:\n\n- driver/fingerprint/elan/elan_sensor.h\n- zephyr/drivers/fingerprint/fingerprint_elan80series_private.h\n\nGiven this, could you clarify what change is being expected here? Are you suggesting consolidating the headers across legacy EC and Zephyr EC, or is there a specific maintenance concern you’d like to address?",
      "parentUuid": "ede41d9a_a3164af2",
      "revId": "d88db1fba163aca7fb6aee481250a27e2a450f3a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2a29d236_7e87611c",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 3698372
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-30T04:24:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, the Zephyr test issue has been resolved.\n\nThe issue was caused by an earlier change made based on that [comment](https://chrome-internal-review.googlesource.com/c/chromeos/vendor/fingerprint/egis/+/9106841/comment/17ba1d86_090a2c5c/), where the\n`buf_size` validation was moved into the private library.\nHowever, the private library is not loaded in the ZTEST env, which caused the tests to fail.\n\nThe current approach is to keep the detailed validation in the private library,\nwhile also retaining the original size check at the caller side.\nThis ensures that ZTEST can still pass.",
      "parentUuid": "405f666f_bb6684c9",
      "revId": "d88db1fba163aca7fb6aee481250a27e2a450f3a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
