    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6ce39be9_f2a7988d",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/fingerprint/Kconfig",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 26,
      "author": {
        "id": 1541085
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-29T15:33:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Instead of hardcoding 26200, use a descriptive calculation in the header:\n\n```\n/* \n * Data Collection Format: \n * Matcher(5120) + Metadata(20) + Raw(10530) + BKG(10530) \u003d 26200 \n */\n#define EGIS_COLLECTION_FORMAT_SIZE (5120 + 20 + 10530 + 10530)\n#define FP_SENSOR_IMAGE_SIZE_EGIS EGIS_COLLECTION_FORMAT_SIZE\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 26,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 26,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "d88db1fba163aca7fb6aee481250a27e2a450f3a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "76025393_8c6d204e",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/fingerprint/Kconfig",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 26,
      "author": {
        "id": 3698372
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-30T04:24:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I’m fine with using a descriptive calculation instead of hardcoding 26200.\n\nFrom what I’ve seen, apart from Elan—which describes a similar breakdown in the\nhelp description—I haven’t found other vendors adding explicit comments or\nmacros that explain how the final image size is calculated. Most implementations\nsimply define the resulting size directly.\n\nIf you agree that adding vendor-specific explanatory comments here is appropriate\nand improves readability and maintainability, then I’m okay with doing so.\nFor example,\n```\n\t# { 8bit image (5120) + metadata (20) + RAW (10530) + BKG (10530) }\n\tdefault 26200if FINGERPRINT_SENSOR_EGIS630\n```",
      "parentUuid": "6ce39be9_f2a7988d",
